From: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Subject: [PATCH] Map files privately

A read-only mapping reads the same whether it is shared or private, but
without an MMU most filesystems can only give a private one, a copy:
shared, every keymap and rules file failed with ENODEV.

Signed-off-by: Tim Douglas <me@timdoug.com>
Upstream: not submitted

--- a/src/utils.c
+++ b/src/utils.c
@@ -30,7 +30,7 @@
     if (fstat(fd, &stat_buf) != 0)
         return false;
 
-    string = mmap(NULL, stat_buf.st_size, PROT_READ, MAP_SHARED, fd, 0);
+    string = mmap(NULL, stat_buf.st_size, PROT_READ, MAP_PRIVATE, fd, 0);
     if (string == MAP_FAILED)
         return false;
 
